  "deltas": {
    "decisions": [
      {
        "action": "replace",
        "decision_id": "D000929",
        "disposition": "existing_equivalent",
        "rationale": "Stacks now proves all three assertions of Lemma 5.6.1 for an injective G-O-module B: q_*^G SheafHom_O(A,B) is flasque on Y, Hom_O(A,B) is right acyclic for G-invariants, and the internal Hom is right acyclic for Gamma_X^G. It also proves the underlying abelian internal-Hom sheaf flasque and explicitly makes no false claim that the global Hom module is injective.",
        "review_state": "integrated_source_stacks_and_independent_review",
        "stacks_labels": "cohomology-lemma-equivariant-hom-injective-acyclic",
        "supersedes": "D000622",
        "unit_id": "tohoku:lemma:5.6.1"
      },
      {
        "action": "replace",
        "decision_id": "D000930",
        "disposition": "existing_equivalent",
        "rationale": "Stacks now identifies each orbit product prod_{x in y} H_x canonically with Coind_{G_y}^G(H_y), proves the Shapiro isomorphisms H^n(G,Coind_{G_y}^G(M))=H^n(G_y,M), and proves that arbitrary products preserve this acyclicity. This is exactly the source's clean coinduced-Hom module step; the separate erroneous quotient-product formula remains open under D000590.",
        "review_state": "integrated_source_stacks_and_independent_review",
        "stacks_labels": "cohomology-lemma-equivariant-product-internal-hom",
        "supersedes": "D000578",
        "unit_id": "tohoku:construction:coinduced-hom-module"
      },
      {
        "action": "replace",
        "decision_id": "D000931",
        "disposition": "existing_equivalent",
        "rationale": "Stacks now proves the corollary for an arbitrary ring R with G-action and semilinear left R-modules A and B: if B is injective in the equivariant module category, then Hom_R(A,B) is right acyclic for invariants in every positive degree. It also retains the source's warning that this Hom module need not be injective.",
        "review_state": "integrated_source_stacks_and_independent_review",
        "stacks_labels": "cohomology-lemma-skew-group-hom-injective-acyclic",
        "supersedes": "D000598",
        "unit_id": "tohoku:corollary:coinduced-hom-acyclicity"
      },
      {
        "action": "replace",
        "decision_id": "D000932",
        "disposition": "existing_equivalent",
        "rationale": "Stacks now defines the source's auxiliary coinduced object B' as prod_{g in G} B, equivalently Map(G,B), and gives its formulas (r f)_g=g(r)f_g and (h f)_g=f_{gh}; this is the same definition expressed without separate crossed-product notation.",
        "review_state": "integrated_source_stacks_and_independent_review",
        "stacks_labels": "cohomology-lemma-skew-group-hom-injective-acyclic",
        "supersedes": "D000603",
        "unit_id": "tohoku:definition:coinduced-module-b-prime"
      },
      {
        "action": "replace",
        "decision_id": "D000933",
        "disposition": "existing_equivalent",
        "rationale": "Stacks now verifies that the displayed formulas make B' a compatible semilinear equivariant R-module and that eta:B->B', eta(b)_g=gb, is an injective equivariant map; injectivity of B then splits eta, exactly giving the source's U-module construction and direct-summand reduction.",
        "review_state": "integrated_source_stacks_and_independent_review",
        "stacks_labels": "cohomology-lemma-skew-group-hom-injective-acyclic",
        "supersedes": "D000579",
        "unit_id": "tohoku:construction:coinduced-u-module-b-prime"
      }
    ],
