    "source_issues": [
      {
        "claim": "The printed formula H_y=prod_{q(x)=y}(H_x)^{G_x} is false: it repeats one stabilizer-fixed factor for every point of a single orbit, whereas an invariant family on that orbit is determined by one representative and gives H_{xi(y)}^{G_{xi(y)}}.",
        "control": "Preserve the printed product diplomatically. In corrected French, English, and semantic source replace it by (prod_{q(x)=y}H_x)^G congruent H_{xi(y)}^{G_{xi(y)}} and hence one factor per orbit; keep D000590 open until that no-overwrite source correction is admitted, then append a resolving mapping successor.",
        "evidence": "Official Part II SHA-256 8D632A04EE0FA987B40B721BEE6E64BB3E641D6A1CE02335556213F1564C9A53, printed p. 215. For G=C2 acting freely and transitively on two points with H_x=Z and identity transport, (prod_{x in y}H_x)^G is the diagonal Z, while the printed product of stabilizer-fixed groups is Z x Z. The corrective Stacks lemma proves the one-factor formula.",
        "evidence_labels": "cohomology-lemma-equivariant-product-internal-hom",
        "issue_id": "I000020",
        "kind": "source_orbit_product_overcount",
        "resolution_decision": "",
        "status": "confirmed",
        "unit_id": "tohoku:construction:product-hom-sheaf"
      },
      {
        "claim": "With the two displayed G-actions and the claimed direction H'->H'', the printed formula psi(f)(g)=g f(g) is not G-equivariant; the equivariant formula in that direction is psi(f)(g)=g^{-1}f(g).",
        "control": "Preserve the printed formula diplomatically. In corrected French, English, and semantic source replace g by g^{-1} in the stated H'->H'' direction; keep D000591 open until that no-overwrite correction is admitted, then append a resolving mapping successor.",
        "evidence": "Official Part II SHA-256 8D632A04EE0FA987B40B721BEE6E64BB3E641D6A1CE02335556213F1564C9A53, printed p. 216. For (h v)_g=v_{gh} and (h star v)_g=h dot v_{gh}, the printed map gives psi(hv)_g=g dot v_{gh}, while (h star psi(v))_g=(hgh) dot v_{gh} in general; with g^{-1}, both sides equal g^{-1} dot v_{gh}. The printed g-formula is equivariant only in the reverse H''->H' direction.",
        "evidence_labels": "cohomology-lemma-skew-group-hom-injective-acyclic",
        "issue_id": "I000021",
        "kind": "source_wrong_coinduction_intertwiner",
        "resolution_decision": "",
        "status": "confirmed",
        "unit_id": "tohoku:construction:two-coinduced-g-actions"
      }
    ],
